8. Best Practices
Least-privilege roles. Start with ACCOUNTADMIN for setup, then create dedicated roles for analysts (read access + agent usage), admins (manage tables, retrain models), and sharing admins (manage cross-agency shares). Apply row-access policies so analysts see only their agency's data.

Dynamic Table refresh cadence. Match TARGET_LAG to your data arrival frequency. Monitor compute cost as you tighten it.

Retrain the Snowpark ML model regularly. Retrain the supplier-failure model quarterly, or whenever confirmed outcomes are updated. Use the Model Registry's versioning to compare performance across retrains before promoting a new version.

Validate Cortex AI outputs periodically. Build a review queue where analysts spot-check COMPLETE explanations and classification outputs against ground truth, and refine prompts based on corrections.

Data sharing governance. Define sharing policies before publishing data to other agencies. Use secure views and row-access policies; audit share usage; restrict PII and classified sourcing details from shared datasets.

CoWork access management. Grant USAGE on the agent deliberately, not to PUBLIC, once this moves beyond a pilot — scope it to the roles that should see this agency's supply chain data.

Start with a pilot. Pick one critical supply chain (e.g., a single defense program or pharmaceutical supply line), load the data, validate the disruption model and risk scores against known outcomes, then expand.

